30
00:01:36,534 --> 00:01:41,415
Because if there's a disagreement later,
proving what was said can be extremely difficult.

31
00:01:41,541 --> 00:01:44,021
So, here are three habits worth adopting.

32
00:01:44,661 --> 00:01:49,781
First, document important discussions,
decisions and employee acknowledgements.

33
00:01:50,581 --> 00:01:55,461
Second, make sure contract cancellations
and off-boarding records match.

34
00:01:55,461 --> 00:01:59,701
There should be a clear record of how and
when the employment relationship ended.

35
00:02:00,261 --> 00:02:04,021
And third, conduct regular HR file audits.

36
00:02:04,021 --> 00:02:08,021
Don't wait until there's a dispute to
discover that important documents are missing.

37
00:02:08,208 --> 00:02:13,088
Good record-keeping protects your
employees, your company, and the decisions you make.

38
00:02:13,728 --> 00:02:18,375
Remember, you may have followed the right
process, but can you prove it?

